   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["DiagramAmplitudeRecords", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Retain explicit diagram expressions, physical propagators and \
numerator assumptions for diagnostics.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DiagramAmplitudeRecords", "[",
         "diagrams", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Build a record for each \
generated diagram without adding an automatic shell reduction."}], "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DiagramAmplitudeRecords", "[",
         "diagrams", ",", " ", "options", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Ap\
ply a supplied pair-preserving simplification and record any declared shell \
usage."}], "Usage"], Cell["Details", "NotesSection"],
  Cell["Each record contains \"OriginalExpression\", \"Expression\", \
\"OriginalNumerator\", \"Numerator\", \"MassRules\", \"ExternalMassRules\", \
\"PhysicalPropagators\" and the physical denominator. This is an inspection \
format rather than the normal user amplitude output.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The option \"SimplificationFunction\" defaults to Identity and \
receives {massRules, expression}. It must return that form with exactly the \
same mass rules. Propagator objects are protected during the transformation."\
, "Notes"], Cell["\"NumeratorOnShellChannels\" records any internal \
conditions used by the supplied transformation; merely declaring them does \
not apply them. \"DenominatorsKeptOffShell\" distinguishes numerator \
simplification from a residue restriction.", "Notes"],
  Cell["For routine bounded simplification and completion, PrepareAmplitudes \
with \"ReturnDetails\" -> True is the richer workflow because it retains \
discarded remainders and selected reference choices.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"SimplificationFunction\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Identity"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Transformation applied to each \
DiagramAmplitudeRecords pair {massRules, expression}. Identity leaves it \
unchanged; a custom function must preserve exactly the same mass rules, with \
propagators protected.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"NumeratorOnShellChannels\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Declarations recording internal shell conditions \
used by a supplied DiagramAmplitudeRecords simplification function. Recording \
them does not itself apply those conditions or change denominators.",
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment ->
      {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Left}}, GridBoxItemSize ->
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.23], Scaled[0.19], Scaled[0.58]}},
     GridBoxDividers -> {"Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}}]],
   "3ColumnTableMod"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
